(KCC 6.2.123).</description><styleUrl>#p_dam</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.95583,47.70398,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Spokane Street Bridge (Post Falls)</name><description>Bridge — Closure signs on the bridge mark the seasonal No Entry zone downstream of it. Vertical clearance not verified.</description><styleUrl>#p_bridge</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.94878,47.7045,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>West Harbor Drive bridge (Harbor Island back channel)</name><description>Bridge — Low bridge over the back channel; vertical clearance not verified.</description><styleUrl>#p_bridge</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.87277,47.69444,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>US-95 bridge over the Spokane River</name><description>Bridge — No-wake from the lake to 300 ft downstream of this bridge (KCC 6.2.122(A)(1)(a)). ITD posts signs and buoys showing where to pass under during work.</description><styleUrl>#p_bridge</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.79936,47.68605,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>US-95 bridge over Blackwell Slough</name><description>Bridge — Upstream end of the Blackwell Island Canal no-motor zone.</description><styleUrl>#p_bridge</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.80652,47.68131,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Q'emiln Park boat launch (City of Post Falls)</name><description>Boat launch — Two-lane ramp below the Spokane Street Bridge; opens with Avista summer operations (mid/late June). Idle under the bridge to reach the river. Fees and hours: check the City of Post Falls.</description><styleUrl>#p_launch</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.9531,47.70351,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Greensferry boat launch (Kootenai County)</name><description>Boat launch — County launch on the south bank, inside Greensferry Bay; closed 10 p.m.–5 a.m. At the county dock: moor no more than 48 h in any 72, no rafting, quiet hours 10 p.m.–8 a.m. (KCC 6.2.122(B)). Surface and fees reported, not verified — check before bringing a heavy wakeboat.</description><styleUrl>#p_launch</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.91909,47.69225,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Blackwell Island boat launch (BLM)</name><description>Boat launch — Inside the lake-approach no-wake zone. The Blackwell Island Canal upstream is no-motor except from 50 ft above this launch down to the river (KCC 6.2.122(A)(2)(d)). Shallow flats off the ramp at low water.</description><styleUrl>#p_launch</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.80538,47.68627,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Hagadone Marine boat ramp (Blackwell Slough)</name><description>Boat launch — Private/marina ramp in the slough — no-motor rules apply in the canal (KCC 6.2.122(A)(2)(d)).</description><styleUrl>#p_launch</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.80577,47.68003,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Q'emiln Park</name><description>Park / beach — City park with swim beach — swimmers likely in summer.</description><styleUrl>#p_park</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.95089,47.70306,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Falls Park (City of Post Falls / Avista)</name><description>Park / beach — Shore park by the dam (below the reach).</description><styleUrl>#p_park</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.95283,47.70911,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Black Bay Park (City of Post Falls)</name><description>Park / beach — Shore access only — Black Bay itself is a no-motor zone (KCC 6.2.122).</description><styleUrl>#p_park</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.92697,47.70278,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Atlas Mill Park / Atlas Waterfront (City of Coeur d'Alene)</name><description>Park / beach — Waterfront park with paddle access.</description><styleUrl>#p_park</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.8165,47.69559,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ross Point Day Use Site (BLM)</name><description>Park / beach — BLM day-use site on the north bank: roped swim area and a floating dock for fishing and non-motorized craft. Swimmers and paddlers likely in summer.</description><styleUrl>#p_park</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.8725,47.70009,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Rodkey Drive shore access (Kootenai County)</name><description>Park / beach — 10-ft public pathway to the north bank — carry-in access only. Closed 10 p.m.–5 a.m. (KCC 6.2.122(B)).</description><styleUrl>#p_park</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.92,47.6968,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Q'emiln Park restrooms</name><description>Restroom / pump-out — Restrooms near the launch.</description><styleUrl>#p_restroom</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.95046,47.70232,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Templin's pump-out (private)</name><description>Restroom / pump-out — Pump-out reported at the marina; confirm availability.</description><styleUrl>#p_restroom</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.94286,47.7021,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Post Falls Landing marina (River's Edge)</name><description>Marina / slips — Slips and docks — structures for the setback rules. — Counts as a structure for the distance rules.</description><styleUrl>#p_marina</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.95072,47.70607,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Blackwell Island Marina (Hagadone Marine Group)</name><description>Marina / slips — Marina in the Blackwell Island Canal by the lake. Powerboats reach the lake from here, not the river — the canal north of the US-95 bridge is no-motor (KCC 6.2.122(A)(2)(d)). — Counts as a structure for the distance rules.</description><styleUrl>#p_marina</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.80619,47.67891,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Templin's Marina</name><description>Marina / slips — Slips and docks — the whole marina counts as structures. — Counts as a structure for the distance rules. — From OpenStreetMap.</description><styleUrl>#p_marina</styleUrl><Polygon><tessellate>1</tessellate><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>-116.9449981,47.704321,0 -116.9457814,47.703711,0 -116.9430488,47.7018584,0 -116.9423129,47.7022685,0 -116.9424046,47.7023604,0 -116.9425395,47.7025363,0 -116.9428803,47.7027992,0 -116.9428995,47.702898,0 -116.9431191,47.703201,0 -116.9436724,47.7036782,0 -116.9440718,47.703981,0 -116.9444212,47.7041683,0 -116.9447911,47.7042982,0 -116.9449235,47.704309,0 -116.9449981,47.704321,0</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>Templin's fuel dock</name><description>Fuel dock — Reported as the only fuel on the reach. Hours not verified. — Counts as a structure for the distance rules.</description><styleUrl>#p_fuel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.94286,47.7021,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Blackwell Island Marina fuel dock</name><description>Fuel dock — Fuel reported at the marina (verify). — Counts as a structure for the distance rules.</description><styleUrl>#p_fuel</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.80619,47.67891,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Fun Unlimited Post Falls (rentals)</name><description>Rentals / dining / services — Boat and PWC rentals (verify season and hours).</description><styleUrl>#p_services</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.94233,47.7023,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Red Lion Templin's restaurant &amp; marina grill</name><description>Rentals / dining / services — Boat-in dining at the marina.</description><styleUrl>#p_services</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.9426,47.70273,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Cedars Floating Restaurant</name><description>Rentals / dining / services — Boat-in dining at the lake end of the slough.</description><styleUrl>#p_services</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.80467,47.67592,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Rock outcrop at the head of Black Bay</name><description>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag) — Mapped rock outcrop (OpenStreetMap). Inside the no-motor zone.</description><styleUrl>#p_hazard</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.92759,47.70381,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Green's Ferry bridge site (demolished)</name><description>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag) — A bridge once crossed here; old pilings may remain below the surface. Unverified.</description><styleUrl>#p_hazard</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.9156,47.69641,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Shallow flats off the Blackwell Island launch</name><description>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag) — Shallow at fall/winter levels (2004 contours).</description><styleUrl>#p_hazard</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.80524,47.68665,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Shallow spot west of Black Bay</name><description>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag) — Under ~5 ft at full pool in the 2004 contours — shallower at fall/winter levels. Screening only; not field-checked. — Derived from the 2004 depth survey.</description><styleUrl>#p_hazard</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.93085,47.70168,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Shallow spot off the south bank</name><description>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag) — Under ~5 ft at full pool in the 2004 contours — shallower at fall/winter levels. Screening only; not field-checked. — Derived from the 2004 depth survey.</description><styleUrl>#p_hazard</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.90863,47.69795,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Shallow spot opposite Ross Point</name><description>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag) — Under ~5 ft at full pool in the 2004 contours — shallower at fall/winter levels. Screening only; not field-checked. — Derived from the 2004 depth survey.</description><styleUrl>#p_hazard</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.89858,47.69694,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Shallow shelf off the south bank west of Harbor Island</name><description>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag) — Water under ~5 ft reaches about 50 m out from the south bank here (2004 contours, full pool). Shallower at fall/winter levels. — Derived from the 2004 depth survey.</description><styleUrl>#p_hazard</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.87685,47.69497,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Shallow bar off Harbor Island's northwest shore</name><description>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag) — Two small under-5-ft spots in 5–10 ft water near the island (2004 contours). Shallower at fall/winter levels. — Derived from the 2004 depth survey.</description><styleUrl>#p_hazard</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.87453,47.69675,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Shallow spot and possible old pilings off the Atlas waterfront</name><description>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag) — One tiny under-5-ft spot in a 15-ft pool (2004 contours). Old log pilings, some submerged, are reported from Cedars to the dam (CdA Press, 2010). — Derived from the 2004 depth survey.</description><styleUrl>#p_hazard</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.82314,47.69739,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Shallow flat off Bellerive</name><description>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag) — Shallow flat about 36 m off the north bank — depths under 10 ft for 70 m around. Boats have hit old pilings in this narrow stretch (CdA Press, 2010). — Derived from the 2004 depth survey.</description><styleUrl>#p_hazard</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.81063,47.69163,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Shallow bar in Greensferry Bay</name><description>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag) — Mid-bay bar about 300 m north of the ramp: a ~1.3 ha area under 10 ft with an under-5-ft core, in 15–25 ft water (2004 contours, full pool). — Derived from the 2004 depth survey.</description><styleUrl>#p_hazard</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.91998,47.69525,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Informal beach (south bank)</name><description>Beach (people in the water) — Informal beach — people may be in the water.</description><styleUrl>#p_beach</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.90726,47.69763,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Ross Point Camp &amp; Conference Center waterfront</name><description>Beach (people in the water) — Private camp waterfront — swimmers and paddlers likely in summer.</description><styleUrl>#p_beach</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.89264,47.69578,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Kiwanis Park swim beach (City of Post Falls)</name><description>Beach (people in the water) — Unguarded city swim beach — swimmers in summer; no wake within 100 ft of people in the water.</description><styleUrl>#p_beach</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.88953,47.69564,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Johnson Mill River Park swim beach</name><description>Beach (people in the water) — Swim beach — swimmers likely in summer.</description><styleUrl>#p_beach</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.84446,47.70039,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>North Idaho College beach</name><description>Beach (people in the water) — Busy swim beach at the river mouth — inside the lake-approach no-wake zone.</description><styleUrl>#p_beach</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.80198,47.67543,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Johnson Mill River Park day-use dock (City of Coeur d'Alene)</name><description>Public / courtesy dock — City day-use dock: no mooring 10 p.m.–6 a.m. or more than 6 hours in any 12; no swimming or wading within 100 ft of the dock (Coeur d'Alene Code §§ 4.20.050–.060). — Counts as a structure for the distance rules.</description><styleUrl>#p_public_dock</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-116.84432,47.70029,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Atlas Mill Park ADA kayak launch</name><description>Public / courtesy dock — Floating paddle launch — paddlers on the water. — Counts as